  "status": "Real stream-create proposal-rejection bug corrected and focused-qualified; combined RPM integration remains required. Historical untraced creation failures remain open.",
  "root_cause": "Metadata leadership can change after the API handler accepts a create request but before Propose checks the term. Propose then returns errNotLeader. The handler discards that error without a response and without recording any assignment that could answer later; the client waits until its original deadline.",
  "fix": "Return the existing typed cluster-unavailable API response (HTTP-style code 503, JetStream error 10008) when the initial stream-create metadata proposal is rejected. Do not track an inflight assignment on failure.",
  "proof": [
    "A real AddStream request reaches the real Raft proposal boundary. The two nonleader API callbacks finish before an actual Raft StepDown; the original proposal then rejects with errNotLeader. All three original controls verify no stream exists and the client reaches its unchanged 30-second deadline.",
    "The permanent regression uses a RaftNode wrapper only to synchronize entry to the unchanged real Propose implementation. No assignment or API reply is fabricated, and no error return is mocked. The wrapper is absent from the runtime build.",
    "The original fails the new exact-API-error regression on all three distributions. Five repetitions per distribution of the fix verify ordinary creation, exact rejection response, absent rejected state and successful fresh creation after real API leadership readiness."
  ],
